<http://data.silknow.org/object/22c2a145-dbc6-3795-9a9b-92ec898c51ce/observation/1>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/technical-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "A woman's gown of beige silk tobine with cream stripes, flecked with red and green spots.  The gown is in the English (tight-back) style, open at the front, and  elbow-length sleeves with double, scalloped and pinked sleeve ruffles. The bodice has pleated robings, decorated with a ruching gathered in the centre over a cord. The bodice and sleeves are lined with bleached linen.  There are six worked eyelets down the front edges of the bodice for fastening.  The pleats at the back are stitched down; the skirt pleated into the waistseam.  Six widths of silk make up the gown; the two front panels are lined with white silk taffeta, and the rest of the skirt faced at the hem with the same.\n\nThe pleats of the front robings have been unpicked, probably for fancy dress in the late 19th century."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/22c2a145-dbc6-3795-9a9b-92ec898c51ce> .

